<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Synthetic test fixture for Dystopo (T24). NOT a recorded track.
  A plausible Skyline Trail loop at Paradise, Mount Rainier National Park (a public, well-known
  hike), clockwise: up past Alta Vista and Glacier Vista to Panorama Point, over the Upper Skyline Trail
  (the high point of the loop), down by the Golden Gate junction, the Stevens-Van Trump memorial and the
  Paradise River, back by Myrtle Falls. Vertices approximate the public trail map (sparse, rounded to
  4 decimals, about 10 m); elevations were sampled from the public DEM at each vertex; times
  come from a pace rule (4.5 km/h flat, +1 min per 10 m up, +1 min per 30 m down) with a 15 minute
  stop at Panorama Point; heart rate and cadence (Garmin TrackPointExtension) are invented.
-->
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Dystopo test fixture (hand-written)"
